hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27610","Haddathana Hashim ibn al-Qasim, he said: Haddathana Abu Ja'far, meaning al-Razi, from Husayn, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Masruq, from Umm Ruman, who is the mother of A'ishah, she said: I and A'ishah were sitting when a woman of the Ansar entered and said: May Allah do to so-and-so and do, meaning her son. She said: So I said to her: What is that? She said: My son was among those who spread the story. She said: So I said to her: What story? She said: Such and such. Then A'ishah said: Did Abu Bakr hear of that? She said: Yes. She said: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hear of that? She said: Yes. So she fell down unconscious, then she awoke with a fever with chills, so I cast clothes over her. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered and said: What is wrong with her? She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, a fever with chills seized her. He said: Perhaps it is from the talk that is being spread. She said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. Then A'ishah raised her head and said: If I speak, you will not excuse me, and if I swear, you will not believe me, and my example and yours is like the example of Ya'qub and his sons when he said: Beautiful patience, and Allah is the One sought for help against what you describe. Then when her exoneration was sent down, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to her and informed her of that, so she said: By the praise of Allah, not by your praise, or she said: nor by the praise of anyone."
"27611","Haddathana Ali ibn Asim, he said: Haddathana Husayn, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from Umm Ruman, she said: While I was with A'ishah, a woman of the Ansar entered upon us and said: May Allah do to her son and do. A'ishah said: Why? She said: He was among those who spread the story. A'ishah said: And what story? She said: Such and such. She said: And has that reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? She said: Yes. And it reached Abu Bakr? She said: Yes. She said: So A'ishah fell unconscious, and she did not awake except with a fever with chills upon her. She said: So I stood and wrapped her up. She said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered and said: What is the matter with her? She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a fever with chills seized her. He said: Perhaps it is concerning talk being spread. She said: So A'ishah sat up for him and said: By Allah, if I swear to you, you will not believe me, and if I excuse myself to you, you will not excuse me, so my example and yours is like the example of Ya'qub and his sons, and Allah is the One sought for help against what you describe. She said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out. She said: And Allah sent down her exoneration, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned, with him Abu Bakr, and he entered and said: O A'ishah, Allah, mighty and majestic, has sent down your exoneration. She said: By the praise of Allah, not by your praise. She said: Abu Bakr said to her: Do you say this to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? She said: Yes. She said: Among those who spread the story was a man whom Abu Bakr used to support, so Abu Bakr swore that he would not join him again, then Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: Let not those of virtue among you and affluence swear, to the end of the verse. Abu Bakr said: Yes indeed, and he joined him again."
